pulsar-client is a shaded uber-jar, so its dependencies do not appear in a
dependency report and have to be read out of the artifact. Its shaded contents
were audited for 4.0.11: Jackson, Caffeine, Guava, gson, re2j, error-prone,
j2objc, completable-futures, Jakarta Activation, netty and netty-reactive-
streams, DataSketches, airlift-compress, swagger-annotations, fastutil,
JCIP annotations, async-http-client, checkerframework, reactive-streams,
RoaringBitmap, SnakeYAML and Circe. All permissive (Apache-2.0, MIT, BSD, EDL,
CC-BY), with javax.annotation carrying the usual CDDL / GPL-2.0-with-classpath-
exception dual licence whose exception removes the copyleft obligation. No
LGPL or GPL code is shaded in, and the jar contains no GPL or LGPL strings.

Note that the shaded jar ships without META-INF/LICENSE or META-INF/NOTICE, so
the attribution for those libraries does not travel with the artifact. The list
above is this project's record of it.


================================================================================
Container images
================================================================================

The backing stores run as their own containers and are pulled, not linked. They
are separate programs communicating over the network, so their licences apply to
those images rather than to DataHub.

Neo4j Community Edition 5.26
    Copyright Neo4j Sweden AB
    GNU General Public License v3.0
    https://github.com/neo4j/docker-neo4j
    deploy/neo4j/Dockerfile builds on `docker.io/library/neo4j:5.26.26`. The
    unsuffixed tag is Community Edition; Enterprise is published under the
    separate `-enterprise` tag and is not used here. DataHub talks to it over
    Bolt as a client, so no GPL linkage arises.

    The image adds one file: the pinned APOC Core plugin jar
    (apoc-5.26.27-core.jar), Copyright Neo4j Sweden AB, Apache License 2.0.

PostgreSQL, ClickHouse, Apache Pulsar, Valkey, Apache Kvrocks and HashiCorp
Vault are pulled unmodified from their official images. See docker-compose.yml
for the pinned versions.


